use in your chatbot"],["en","what technologies are used"],["en","which technology did you use"],["en","tech stack of chatbot"],["en","how does your chatbot work"],["en","how does the chatbot work"],["en","explain chatbot architecture"],["en","working of your project"],["en","what challenges did you face"],["en","what was the biggest challenge"],["en","challenges in your project"],["en","problems faced in chatbot"],["en","what are future improvements"],["en","future scope of chatbot"],["en","how can you improve the chatbot"],["en","what would you add next"],["en","tell me about yourself"],["en","introduce yourself"],["en","tell me something about yourself"],["en","give me your introduction"],["en","who are you"],["en","what are your strengths"],["en","tell me your strengths"],["en","what are your key strengths"],["en","your strengths"],["en","what is your weakness"],["en","tell me your weakness"],["en","what are your weaknesses"],["en","your weakness"],["en","what is your career goal"],["en","where do you see yourself"],["en","what are your career goals"],["en","what do you want to become"],["en","why should we hire you"],["en","why should we hire you"],["en","why are you suitable for this role"],["en","why should we select you"],["en","can you work in a team"],["en","how do you work in a team"],["en","are you a team player"],["en","tell me about teamwork"],["en","how do you handle pressure"],["en","can you work under pressure"],["en","how do you handle stress"],["en","working under pressure"],["en","why do you want to join our company"],["en","why this company"],["en","why do you want to work here"],["en","why should you join us"],["en","why software development"],["en","why did you choose software engineering"],["en","why did you choose computer science"],["en","why do you like software development"],["en","tell me about a failure"],["en","what is your biggest failure"],["en","how do you handle failure"],["en","tell me about a mistake"],["en","how do you handle conflict"],["en","what if you disagree with your teammate"],["en","how do you resolve conflicts"],["en","team conflict"],["en","how do you learn new technology"],["en","how do you learn new skills"],["en","how do you keep yourself updated"],["en","how do you learn"],["en","what are your hobbies"],["en","tell me about your hobbies"],["en","what do you do in your free time"],["en","your hobbies"],["en","bye"],["en","goodbye"],["en","see you later"],["en","exit"],["en","quit"]]},"ner":{"settings":{"tag":"ner","entityPreffix":"%","entitySuffix":"%"},"rules":{}},"nlgManager":{"settings":{"tag":"nlg-manager"},"responses":{"en":{"greeting":[{"answer":"Hello! How can I help you?"},{"answer":"Hi! What would you like to know?"}],"java":[{"answer":"Java is a high-level, object-oriented programming language known for platform independence, security, robustness, and its large ecosystem."}],"oops":[{"answer":"The four main OOP concepts are Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, and Abstraction."}],"python":[{"answer":"Python is a high-level, interpreted programming language known for its simple syntax and extensive libraries. It is widely used in web development, automation, data science, AI, and machine learning."}],"javascript":[{"answer":"JavaScript is a programming language mainly used to create interactive web applications. It can run in browsers and on servers using Node.js."}],"cpp":[{"answer":"C++ is a general-purpose programming language that supports object-oriented, procedural, and generic programming. It is widely used for system software, competitive programming, and performance-intensive applications."}],"html":[{"answer":"HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. It provides the structure and content of web pages using elements such as headings, paragraphs, forms, links, and images."}],"css":[{"answer":"CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. It is used to style and design HTML elements, including layouts, colors, fonts, spacing, and responsive interfaces."}],"react":[{"answer":"React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces. It uses reusable components and a virtual DOM to efficiently update the UI."}],"nodejs":[{"answer":"Node.js is a JavaScript runtime environment that allows JavaScript to run outside the browser. It is commonly used for building scalable backend applications and APIs."}],"express":[{"answer":"Express.js is a lightweight Node.js framework used to build web applications and REST APIs. It provides routing, middleware, and request-response handling."}],"rest_api":[{"answer":"A REST API allows applications to communicate over HTTP using methods such as GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE. It commonly exchanges data using JSON."}],"sql":[{"answer":"SQL stands for Structured Query Language. It is used to create, read, update, and delete data in relational databases."}],"mongodb":[{"answer":"MongoDB is a NoSQL database that stores data in flexible JSON-like documents. It is commonly used with Node.js applications."}],"array":[{"answer":"An array is a data structure used to store multiple values, usually of the same type, in a contiguous or indexed collection."}],"linked_list":[{"answer":"A linked list is a linear data structure made of nodes where each node stores data and a reference to another node. Common types are singly, doubly, and circular linked lists."}],"stack":[{"answer":"A stack is a linear data structure that follows LIFO, meaning Last In First Out. Common operations are push, pop, and peek."}],"queue":[{"answer":"A queue is a linear data structure that follows FIFO, meaning First In First Out. Common operations are enqueue and dequeue."}],"binary_search":[{"answer":"Binary search finds an element in a sorted collection by repeatedly dividing the search range in half. Its time complexity is O(log n)."}],"sorting":[{"answer":"Sorting arranges data in a particular order. Common algorithms include Bubble Sort, Selection Sort, Insertion Sort, Merge Sort, Heap Sort, and Quick Sort."}],"binary_tree":[{"answer":"A binary tree is a hierarchical data structure in which each node can have at most two children, commonly called the left and right child."}],"machine_learning":[{"answer":"Machine learning is a branch of AI where systems learn patterns from data to make predictions or decisions. Common types include supervised, unsupervised, and reinforcement learning."}],"nlp":[{"answer":"NLP stands for Natural Language Processing. It enables computers to process and understand human language. Applications include chatbots, translation, sentiment analysis, and question answering."}],"node_nlp":[{"answer":"Node-NLP is a JavaScript library for natural language processing. In this chatbot, it is used for intent classification and generating responses based on trained user queries."}],"chatbot_project":[{"answer":"I developed a QnA AI Chatbot using Node.js, Express.js, and Node-NLP. The system accepts user questions, processes them using NLP-based intent classification, and returns relevant answers."}],"project_technology":[{"answer":"The chatbot uses Node.js for the runtime, Express.js for the backend API, Node-NLP for natural language processing, JSON for training data, and HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for the frontend."}],"project_working":[{"answer":"The user enters a question through the frontend. The request is sent to an Express.js API, Node-NLP processes the question and identifies the intent, and the chatbot returns the appropriate response."}],"project_challenge":[{"answer":"One challenge was improving intent recognition for different ways of asking the same question. I addressed this by adding multiple training utterances for each intent and improving the training dataset."}],"project_future":[{"answer":"Future improvements include MongoDB-based chat history, user authentication, an admin dashboard, more training data, confidence scores, better fallback handling, and deployment to the cloud."}],"introduction":[{"answer":"I am a B.Tech Computer Science student with a strong interest in software development, problem solving, backend development, and AI. I have worked with Java, Python, JavaScript, Node.js, React, SQL, and machine learning technologies. I enjoy building practical projects and continuously improving my technical skills."}],"strengths":[{"answer":"My strengths are problem-solving, willingness to learn, consistency, and the ability to understand new technologies quickly. I also try to improve my skills through practical projects and coding practice."}],"weakness":[{"answer":"One area I am working on is improving my communication skills. I am actively practicing English communication and focusing on explaining technical concepts more clearly and confidently."}],"career_goal":[{"answer":"My goal is to become a skilled software engineer who can design reliable and scalable applications, solve challenging problems, and contribute effectively to a technology-driven organization."}],"why_hire":[{"answer":"You should hire me because I have a strong foundation in programming and software development, practical project experience, a willingness to learn, and the ability to adapt to new technologies. I am motivated to contribute to the team while continuously improving my skills."}],"teamwork":[{"answer":"Yes, I am comfortable working in a team. I believe good teamwork requires clear communication, responsibility, listening to others, and supporting team members when solving problems."}],"pressure":[{"answer":"I handle pressure by breaking the problem into smaller tasks, prioritizing important work, and focusing on solving one problem at a time. I also communicate early if I face a blocker."}],"why_company":[{"answer":"I want to join a company where I can apply my technical skills to real-world problems, learn from experienced professionals, contribute to meaningful projects, and grow as a software engineer."}],"why_software":[{"answer":"I chose software development because I enjoy problem-solving and building applications that can solve real-world problems. I also like that technology continuously evolves and provides opportunities to keep learning."}],"failure":[{"answer":"I see failures as opportunities to learn. When something does not work, I analyze the cause, identify what I could have done better, and apply that learning to the next task."}],"conflict":[{"answer":"I try to understand the other person's perspective first. Then I discuss the issue using facts and focus on finding a solution that is best for the project rather than making it personal."}],"learning":[{"answer":"I usually start with official documentation and basic concepts, then build a small practical project. After that, I solve problems and gradually work on more advanced use cases."}],"hobbies":[{"answer":"My hobbies include reading, writing, and singing. These activities help me stay creative and relaxed."}],"goodbye":[{"answer":"Goodbye! Have a great day."},{"answer":"Thank you for chatting. See you soon!"}]}}},"actionManager":{"settings":{"tag":"action-manager"},"actions":{}},"slotManager":{}}